ns. Perineurial cells historically have been referred to as fibroblasts because of shape; however, unlike fibroblasts, a perineurial cell: does not have a compact nucleus and large endoplasmic reticulum; does have a double basement membrane opposed to a single basal lamina; is carefully joined to other perineurial cells by tight junctions into a single sheet as opposed to arranged in a large mass; and finally, can surround a small axon bundle at a nerve terminal whereas a fibroblast cannot.\")\n\n  Line 19958: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36244793\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0002576 \"There are studies that largely accept the idea that the perineurial cell is a modified fibroblast with myofibroblastic features.\")\n\n  Line 20362: # Class: obo:CL_0002620 (skin fibroblast)\n\n  Line 20364: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002620 \"A fibroblast of skin.\")\n\n  Line 20369: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002620 \"skin fibroblast\")\n\n  Line 22850: # Class: obo:CL_0008023 (obsolete cardiac fibroblast)\n\n  Line 22854: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0008023 \"obsolete cardiac fibroblast\")\n\n  Line 23942: # Class: obo:CL_0009078 (thymic fibroblast type 1)\n\n  Line 23944: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32079746\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009078 \"A fibroblast located in the thymic capsule.\")\n\n  Line 23947: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0009078 \"thymic capsular fibroblast\")\n\n  Line 23948: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0009078 \"thymic fibroblast type 1\")\n\n  Line 23952: # Class: obo:CL_0009079 (thymic fibroblast type 2)\n\n  Line 23954: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32079746\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009079 \"A fibroblast located between thymic lobules.\")\n\n  Line 23957: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0009079 \"thymic interlobular fibroblast\")\n\n  Line 23958: Anno