College and Hospital, Bhimavaram, India.\n\n-   PMID: **22529592**\n-   PMCID: [PMC3329689](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3329689/)\n-   DOI: [10.4103/0973-029X.84516](https://doi.org/10.4103/0973-029x.84516)\n\nItem in Clipboard\n\nFull text links Cite\n\nDisplay options\n\nDisplay options\n\nFormat AbstractPubMedPMID\n\n## Abstract\n\nFibroblasts are a major stromal cell type present in human connective tissue maintaining the structural integrity in health. Depending on the situation, location and various conditions, fibroblasts exhibit considerable variation in morphology, size and shape that suggest the existence of discrete cellular subsets. The purpose of this short communication is to provide information regarding the heterogenecity of fibroblasts and its variability in physiological and pathological conditions.\n\n**Keywords:** Fibroblasts; fibrocytes; giant cell fibroblasts; myofibroblasts.\n\n[PubMed Disclaimer](/disclaimer/)\n\n## Conflict of interest statement\n\nConflict of Interest: None declared.\n\n## Figures\n\n [![Figure 1](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/blobs/ac53/3329689/695f8117732a/JOMFP-15-247-g001.gif)](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/blobs/ac53/3329689/f738f804b710/JOMFP-15-247-g001.jpg) \n\n**\n\nFigure 1\n\n**\n\nActive fibroblasts, 20×\n\n**\n\nFigure 1\n\n**\n\nActive fibroblasts, 20×\n\n**Figure 1**\n\nActive fibroblasts, 20×\n\n [![Figure 2](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/blobs/ac53/3329689/1424c73691d5/JOMFP-15-247-g002.gif)](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/blobs/ac53/3329689/94b9464cb68a/JOMFP-15-247-g002.jpg) \n\n**\n\nFigure 2\n\n**\n\nVimentin positive, 20×\n\n**\n\nFigure 2\n\n**\n\nVimentin positive, 20×\n\n**Figure 2**\n\nVimentin positive, 20×\n\n [![Figure 3](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/blobs/ac53/3329689/677f65fac81b/JOMFP-15-247-g003.gif)](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/blobs/ac53/3329689/89d75fefce38/JOMFP-15-247-g003.jpg) \n\n**\n\nFigure 3\n\n**\n\nInactive fibroblasts, 20×\n\n**\n\nFigure 3\n\n**